              <span class="lvg-truth-chapters__refusal-heading">
                What this argument does not say
              </span>

            


            

              <div class="lvg-truth-chapters__refusal-content">
                <p>That every product harms skin. Most do exactly what they say they do. The critique is of the&nbsp;<em>number</em>&nbsp;of them, and of the incentive that keeps adding one more.</p><p>That fewer ingredients are better. LNGVTY's formulas are ingredient-dense by design. The unit that has to come down is the product and the step, never the molecule.</p><p>That the industry is acting in bad faith. It is acting on its incentives, which is a harder problem and a more honest one to name.</p><p>That you should have spotted it. The loop is legible from outside it and very nearly invisible from within.</p>
              </div>

            


            

